00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:51.240
channel. Whenever a customer reaches out

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.120
to us to get help on their problem, we

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:55.080
directly ask them, "Send us your file.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:57.520
We will record a custom tutorial or

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:59.480
custom loom video for you." And at times

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:01.200
we also get on a call with our customers

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:03.000
and we walk them through their workflow

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:05.120
and solve the problem on the call. We

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:08.000
record all this conversation and over

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:10.360
the span of 3 years we have over 1,500

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:12.400
recorded videos and these videos are

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:14.640
gold mine for us. People talk about the

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:17.000
real problem, the edge cases that never

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:19.200
come up in search keyword results or

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.680
anywhere. And we create content around

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.640
those support calls. And the fourth

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:25.000
touchpoint for harvesting customer pain

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:27.640
is YouTube comments. I go to my niche,

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:29.000
find out videos that has not high views

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.120
but high number of comments. High

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.440
comments signals customer pain which is

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:35.719
unresolved and then make a list of all

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:37.360
the objections that the customers have

00:08:35.719 --> 00:08:39.240
and then I simply create a better

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.159
content around that answering all those

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.200
objections.

